diff -ruN a/templates/skills/feature/reference/test-task.md b/templates/skills/feature/reference/test-task.md
--- a/templates/skills/feature/reference/test-task.md	1969-12-31 19:00:00.000000000 -0500
+++ b/templates/skills/feature/reference/test-task.md	2026-11-13 09:43:36.317073510 -0500
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Test task package (Phase 4 step 1)
+
+Read this before launching `test-writer` for the test task.
+
+The test task is black-box: `test-writer` writes tests from the task spec and the public
+interface of the code under test, never from its implementation.
+
+Before the launch, write `_memory/work/goals/[goal]/briefs/NN-interfaces.md` (NN = the
+test task's number): for every module under test, its exported signatures, docstrings and
+public types, extracted with a definitions search (for example
+`rg -n '^(def|class|export|func|public) '` plus the docstring lines that follow), never
+whole function bodies.
+
+`## Files to Read` for the test task lists:
+
+- that brief file, the test task file with its `## Acceptance Criteria`, and the
+  implementation tasks' acceptance criteria;
+- existing tests, fixtures and the test-framework configuration, to match conventions;
+- matching path-scoped rule files and `{{IDE_DIR}}/skills/test-ladder/SKILL.md`.
+
+It lists no module path. The `## Rules` section of the package states: `test-writer`
+reads no module under test, except after its tests are written, to read a function body
+only to make the injected edit a regression proof needs.
